inst Calum Ritchie","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:26"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"21"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"2993474","displayName":"Colton Sissons","shortName":"C. Sissons"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"5149210","displayName":"Calum Ritchie","shortName":"C. Ritchie"}}]},{"id":"401892523000000760","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Gavin McKenna Snap Shot saved by Ilya Sorokin","type":{"id":"506","text":"Shot","abbreviation":"shot-on-goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:46"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"21"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5342529","displayName":"Gavin McKenna","shortName":"G. McKenna"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"3151981","displayName":"Ilya Sorokin","shortName":"I. Sorokin"},"type":"saver"}]},{"id":"401892523000000930","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Nick Blankenburg hit Calum Ritchie","type":{"id":"503","text":"Hit","abbreviation":"hit"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:52"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"21"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4781550","displayName":"Nick Blankenburg","shortName":"N. Blankenburg"},"type":"hit-credited"},{"athlete":{"id":"5149210","displayName":"Calum Ritchie","shortName":"C. Ritchie"},"type":"hitted"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1838","fullName":"Scotiabank Arena","address":{"city":"Toronto","country":"Canada"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1838.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":18915,"officials":[{"fullName":"Mark Shewchyk","displayName":"Mark Shewchyk","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Shandor Alphonso","displayName":"Shandor Alphonso","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Pierre Lambert","displayName":"Pierre Lambert","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Mike Sullivan","displayName":"Mike Sullivan","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Bo Horvat scores winner and adds assist in Islanders' 4-1 win over Maple Leafs","description":"— Bo Horvat scored the winner and added an assist to help the New York Islanders beat the Toronto Maple Leafs 4-1 on Saturday night.","story":"TORONTO -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042002/bo-horvat\">Bo Horvat</a> scored the winner and added an assist to help the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyi/new-york-islanders\">New York Islanders</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/tor/toronto-maple-leafs\">Toronto Maple Leafs</a> 4-1 on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565244/simon-holmstrom\">Simon Holmstrom</a> scored twice, the second into an empty net, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042086/anthony-duclair\">Anthony Duclair</a> also connected for New York (4-3-1). <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3151981/ilya-sorokin\">Ilya Sorokin</a> made 28 saves.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2993474/colton-sissons\">Colton Sissons</a> replied for Toronto (3-4-2). <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5571/sergei-bobrovsky\">Sergei Bobrovsky</a> stopped 16 shots for the Maple Leafs. They have dropped three straight games and four of their last five.\n\n\r\n              The Islanders jumped out to a 1-0 lead at 8:18 of the first period when Duclair took a pass in the slot and changed the angle before firing through a partial screen on Bobrovsky.\n\n\r\n              Coming off a hat trick Thursday night in a 5-4 home shootout loss to Buffalo, Maple Leafs winger <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587996/kirill-marchenko\">Kirill Marchenko</a> had a couple of chances that Sorokin turned aside in the second.\n\n\r\n              No. 1 overall pick <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5342529/gavin-mckenna\">Gavin McKenna</a>, who was benched for the second half of Thursday’s contest, had an opportunity it late in the second period on a partial breakaway, but fired high and wide. The Islanders raced the other way, with Horvat eventually beating Bobrovsky with 1:27 to go.\n\n\r\n              Sissons got Toronto — which topped New York 2-1 at Scotiabank Arena on Sept. 30 — within one at 3:54 of the third on a tipped shot through traffic, but Holmstrom restored the two-goal lead with 5:52 to go off Horvat's setup before firing into the empty net with just over two minutes remaining.\n\n\r\n              The Islanders' <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587580/matias-maccelli\">Matias Maccelli</a> left in the first period and didn’t return with an apparent lower-body injury. The winger, who spent last season with Toronto, stepped on the stick of defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3149843/darren-raddysh\">Darren Raddysh</a> and fell awkwardly.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              <hl2 />\r\n              Islanders: Host Anaheim on Tuesday night\n\n\r\n              Maple Leafs: Host San Jose on Monday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>\r\n              \n\n\r\n              <hl2 />","published":"2026-10-18T01:57:29Z"}}